A||N||1||mbramble||How Do I Find an Exhaust Manifold Leak??||||5||
Z||000000||mbramble||10-31-2000||06:06 PM||||I believe that I have a leak (or leaks) somewhere in the vicinity of the exhaust manifold on my 87 Duke.  I say this because of the sounds I hear in that area.  Plus, since the dogbone and motor mount were in such bad shape, I'm sure the engine has moved around quite a bit for long periods of time and possible cracked something.<P>Is there some 'test' that I can use to pinpoint leaks without removing the exhaust manifold??  Would like to get to the point where the exhaust comes out the tailpipe instead of other places!  I patched up some holes in my cat  (which I will replace soon) and it helped some but there are more leaks and I don't know how to pinpoint them.<P>TIA,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DavidHenshaw||10-31-2000||06:49 PM||||Mike, the only way I've ever heard of pinpointing the leak is to use a short section of flexible rubber hose about 3/8" size and about four feet long. Hold one end of the hose aginst your ear and pass the other end of the hose about the different parts of the manifold as the engine is running. This should give you some idea of where the leak(s) is.<P>Dave<P>86 GT fastback||||reg||1
